#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:5
#: e096c8619a8c4d78a3a7826e6eb5debf
msgid "Traditional Helicopter Tips"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:7
#: 6c2d748f1b9748999741e0629617700f
msgid "Be sure to follow the wiki instructions, step by step!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:8
#: a0e84d057958405f8f496a64cbefa361
msgid "Be sure the CG is in line with the main rotor shaft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:9
#: a9e585cb6ae744bf8d1431863d2d63ff
msgid ""
"Blade tracking must be within a quarter blade thickness or better to "
"avoid excessive vibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:11
#: 787fef1afa674b32a7bfcbfae7755f70
msgid "Vibration is the arch enemy of Helicopter autopilots!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:11
#: 9dcb4d51354b4b949e334b7488f79d37
msgid ""
"Internal Combustion Engines and Turbines can created high frequency "
"vibrations that do not appear in the VIBE logs and can be aliased to low "
"frequencies which can impact EKF and Attitude control (see below for "
"ground tests to check for this). This also often occurs in electric "
"helicopters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:12
#: 7021cd77a9d14686825b33f5337da5e1
msgid ""
"The autopilot should be well isolated for vibration. Using autopilots "
"with internal IMU vibration damping and vibration reducing mounts is "
"recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:13
#: cf84f8ac7c5345b388c25ac30744f48b
msgid ""
"Traditional Helicopter *is* capable of inverted flight and using full "
"negative collective ranges."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:16
#: f9fe96453601431c8d9bc1a21ae2a289
msgid "Checking for High Frequency Vibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:18
#: 4c5f651ec5c94bcf963ca79d47b99fac
msgid ""
"High frequency vibrations in this context are vibrations close to the IMU"
" sampling frequency, or its multiples, which will be aliased down into "
"the same range as control inputs for the attitude controllers. Symptoms "
"of high frequency vibration can be that the attitude estimate becomes "
"incorrect causing it to lean significantly even though the pilot is "
"commanding level flight in stabilized modes. In the extreme, it can "
"result in an :ref:`ekf-inav-failsafe` or even a crash. Excessive "
"vibration can also make altitude hold imprecise or even produce "
"uncontrollable climbs/descents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:20
#: e158b35b5e8a4c52a4962eb66a561033
msgid ""
"One method of testing this, is to secure the helicopter to the ground, "
"and run up the main rotor, watching the artificial horizon in the ground "
"control station. If it moves away from level, you probably have a "
"vibration issue which needs to be addressed. Testing should be done at "
"various collective levels and rotor speeds. Be careful not to over-stress"
" the helicopter with collective extremes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:22
#: 368224e36e81452380c80671fae216af
msgid "Setup for ground test:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:24
#: 43173683966442fcb246cdc5ba1be8e7
msgid "Secure vehicle to the ground."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:25
#: 216a42ea777a41dcb16205b69c3ec11e
msgid ""
"Temporarily reduce Roll, Pitch, and Yaw  P,I,and D, PIDs to zero. Be sure"
" to restore them after this test!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:26
#: bf66c033d014477cb0c2043d94b35558
msgid ""
"Set :ref:`ACRO_OPTIONS<ACRO_OPTIONS>` = 2, temporarily, if not being used"
" already."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:27
#: 067da62979454ee98acfd0c36d89c9cf
msgid "Change to ACRO mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:28
#: f8741a1a9d07460e832d5dba5fa59731
msgid ""
"Arm and engage motor interlock, allowing the vehicle to spool up at 0 "
"degree pitch, watching for any change from level in the GSC of the "
"artificial horizon. Any significant tilt indicates noise is disrupting "
"the attitude estimate and should be investigated and eliminated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:29
#: 39ebc031d35040af896b575f3f45314f
msgid ""
"Change the target main rotor speed a bit above and below the nominal "
"target using the :ref:`H_RSC_SETPOINT<H_RSC_SETPOINT>` (or TX throttle "
"curve if using Passthru mode) and repeat."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:30
#: 85e7ac08e00d4fef8dabd68317914245
msgid "Re-check the blade tracking also while doing this test."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:32
#: 904b9aae279f4d62904187d9e7e4260a
msgid ""
"Be sure to also eliminate the possibility of lower frequency vibrations "
"from the main or tail rotors causing the issue. Unlike vibrations near "
"the sampling rate and its harmonics, which cannot be eliminated by "
"software filtering, rotor vibrations can be improved using ArduPilot's "
"notch filtering feature. See :ref:`common-measuring-vibration` and "
":ref:`Helicopter Dynamic Notch Filter Setup<common-imu-notch-filtering-"
"helicopter-setup>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:35
#: 51379c5d52f14e9999ca5a7fc8ca8e71
msgid "Possible False Landing Detections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-tips.rst:37
#: 31867dd3064640f58a5e8200c9c61260
msgid ""
"Under extreme circumstances (flying in extremely turbulent conditions, "
"for example), it is possible for the firmware, to falsely detect a "
"landing condition, although still flying. This can lead to lack of "
"control in position control modes and even possible disarming. An RC "
"Auxiliary Function (\"159\") is provided to allow an RC to enable (needed"
" when actually landing) or disable (to prevent false detects during "
"missions) the landing detection algorithm under pilot control."
msgstr ""

